          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Three-year-old Arjun uses only a few isolated words and cannot walk steadily without support. Which pair of developmental domains best describes his presenting delays?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Language and gross motor</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Inability to form sentences at 3 years indicates language delay, while an unsteady gait reflects gross motor delay. Delay across two or more domains in a child under five raises the possibility of global developmental delay.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Fine motor and vision</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Arjun's presenting complaints relate to speech and walking — not fine motor manipulation or visual tracking.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Social and cognitive</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>While Arjun's poor eye contact is a social concern noted separately, his stated presenting complaints — few words and unsteady gait — point to language and gross motor delay.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Language and fine motor</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Arjun's walking difficulty is a gross motor deficit (large-muscle balance and locomotion), not a fine motor problem (grasping, drawing).</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review the developmental domains: Arjun's few words indicate language delay, and his unsteady gait indicates gross motor delay."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. Identifying which developmental domains are affected is the first step in characterising a child's delay."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
