          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 2-year-old is brought with suspected developmental delay. Which of the followi</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 2-year-old is brought with suspected developmental delay. Which of the following is NOT one of the four core components of a structured developmental evaluation?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Detailed developmental and birth history</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A detailed history — including prenatal, perinatal, and postnatal events as well as milestone attainment — IS one of the four core evaluation components.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Trial of empirical physiotherapy before further workup</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Physiotherapy is a management intervention, not part of the diagnostic evaluation. The four components are: history, physical and neurological examination, standardised developmental assessment, and directed investigations guided by clinical findings.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Standardised formal developmental assessment</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A standardised assessment IS a core component — it objectively confirms and quantifies the delay across domains.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Directed investigations guided by clinical findings</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Directed investigations (e.g. thyroid function, karyotype, neuroimaging) guided by the clinical picture ARE part of a complete evaluation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The four components of structured developmental evaluation are: (1) detailed history, (2) physical and neurological examination, (3) standardised formal developmental assessment, and (4) directed investigations."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct — therapy is part of management, not evaluation. A structured evaluation comprises history, examination, formal assessment, and directed investigations."
                }
              ],
